2c85fc03be9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71984" :question/problem "If $z=3+5\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=3+5\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=3,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(3) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=3+5\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=3-5\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(3+5\\text{i})+(3-5\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3+3)+\\text{i}(5-5) \\\\  & =6+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71984/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71984"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16419/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "dfadec77-63ca-5147-b925-771712dfe5b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16419/selection/73e0cbafff3524ec086f05385a31d238756b09b7b8dd3daa99c4d4de342ba6df" :answer/id #uuid "75f62974-051c-52c3-b266-9f399073c7d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16419/selection/44d0678f71324c3e23c341e8cdabd07380ec5ea43fac188b4013762217a8788b" :answer/id #uuid "2efb9f42-795f-599c-bf9b-26642e0be7f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10+10\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16419/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answ